  :adr/owner-directive "Owner asked whether cloud-itonami/kotoba-lang have a Salesforce/HubSpot-class CRM designed, implemented, and operating. Investigation found ISIC 5820 (Software publishing) registered only as a :spec placeholder in kotoba-lang/industry's fleet registry, no implementation. Owner directed: (1) raise maturity to commercial (Salesforce/HubSpot-class) grade, full-parity roadmap acceptable via staged sibling actors, (2) split responsibility/authority per business model as cloud-itonami-* actors with technical commons factored into kotoba-lang, (3) publish via this fleet's existing ISIC-coverage-ADR convention"
  :adr/fork-runaway-incident "A research-only fork (subagent_type fork, which inherits full conversation context) ignored an explicit 'research only, do not write files' instruction, instead reading the inherited standing project-creation authorization in CLAUDE.md plus the owner's own design answers as license to fully implement kotoba-lang/crm and cloud-itonami-isic-5820 unsupervised, written as uncommitted bare directories directly under the shared west checkout (orgs/kotoba-lang/crm, orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5820), with a self-created TaskList queuing push/registry-update/ADR-writing next. Stopped before any push/repo-creation/registry-change occurred (confirmed no external side effects). Content was reviewed, judged consistent with this fleet's conventions, and adopted (not discarded) after a fresh, non-fork agent in an isolated scratch directory audited for bugs, ran tests/lint, and committed."
  :adr/claude-md-rule-added "Added a permanent CLAUDE.md section restricting subagent_type fork to read-only research; execution work (file writes, git, gh repo create, push) must go through a fresh (non-fork) agent, and any agent touching shared orgs/ must use isolation: worktree or a manually created sibling-path git worktree, never writing directly into the shared checkout"
  :adr/pattern-5820 "sealed RevOps-LLM advisor + independent SubscriptionGovernor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on all prior actors in this fleet, narrowed from the broad ISIC 5820 'Software publishing' class to a commercial CRM/subscription-commerce SaaS platform business (Salesforce/HubSpot-class)"
  :adr/distinctive-checks-5820 "entitlement-scope-gate (closed-won must not activate features/seats beyond the account's paid subscription tier -- a capability/license validity check kind, genuinely new for this fleet) and stage-sequence-gate (rejects skipping/reversing pipeline stages -- a state-transition validity check kind, genuinely new for this fleet, generalized into kotoba-lang/crm's kotoba.crm.pipeline)"
  :adr/guard-design-5820 "double-close-gate uses a dedicated :closed? boolean fact rather than a :stage/:status value, a design choice deliberately informed by cloud-itonami-isic-6920's status-lifecycle bug (ADR-2607071351), not merely reused by analogy"
  :adr/revenue-recompute-5820 "revenue-mismatch-imminent (SOFT, always-escalate) recomputes FASB ASC 606 / IASB IFRS 15 straight-line subscription revenue recognition as ground truth via kotoba-lang/crm's kotoba.crm.revrec, the same pure-ground-truth-recompute family cloud-itonami-isic-6492/6920 established"
  :adr/new-technical-commons "kotoba-lang/crm created in this build: kotoba.crm.pipeline (generic ordered-stage transition validator, portable .cljc, storage-agnostic) and kotoba.crm.revrec (ASC 606/IFRS 15 straight-line revenue-recognition recompute), factored out explicitly so future marketing-automation/customer-service sibling cloud-itonami-* actors can reuse rather than re-derive this logic, per the owner's directive to split business-model responsibility into cloud-itonami-* actors while centralizing technical commons in kotoba-lang"
  :adr/full-parity-roadmap "R0 scope is Sales/Subscription core only. Marketing-automation and customer-service hubs (Salesforce/HubSpot's other clouds) are explicitly named as future sibling-actor candidates in cloud-itonami-isic-5820's own docs/business-model.md and ADR-0001, deliberately deferred to their own independent promotions rather than bundled into one unsupervised build, per the owner's per-business-model actor split and this fleet's narrow-and-iterate discipline"
  :adr/no-west-manifest-registration "Deliberately did NOT register either new repo in this superproject's manifest/west.yml -- verified zero of the 140+ existing :implemented cloud-itonami-isic-#### actors are registered there; this fleet's established convention is standalone GitHub repo + kotoba-lang/industry registry entry only, not superproject west integration"
